course: dictionary
lesson: 15447
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word stellar has two. The first is about stars in space: «The telescope picked up stellar light from a galaxy far away.» Here stellar links to stars, the bright lights in the night sky.
explain: The second meaning is informal, which means relaxed everyday speech: stellar means excellent or brilliant. «Maya's stellar performance in the school play made everyone clap.» Nobody is talking about space here. It is praise.
explain: How do you know which meaning to use? Read the words around it. Space words like galaxy, light or Sun point to the first meaning. Words like performance, goal or career point to the second. Then swap in your meaning and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Stellar means about stars, or excellent.
fact: The first meaning is used in science, with stars, the Sun and galaxies.
fact: The meaning «excellent» is informal, so you will hear it in sport, news and everyday talk.
fact: A stellar nursery is a cloud in space where new stars form.
fact: Stellar wind is a stream of tiny particles that flows out from a star.
exercise: «The telescope picked up stellar light from a galaxy far away.» What does stellar mean here? | Very quiet | *About stars in space | Made of wood | Excellent and brilliant
exercise: «Her stellar performance won the whole class over.» What does stellar mean here? | Very cold | About the Moon | Slow and boring | *Excellent and brilliant
exercise: «The stellar nursery is a cloud of gas and dust where new stars form.» Find and copy the word that is a clue to the first meaning. | dust | nursery | where | *stars
exercise: test:
test: Zara says, «Jake's stellar goal won the match.» What does stellar mean? | Very small | About stars in space | *Excellent and brilliant | Muddy and wet
test: «Scientists watched a new star being born in a stellar nursery.» What does stellar mean here? | Excellent | Empty and dark | Rough and bumpy | *About stars
exam: «Her stellar career as a singer lasted fifty years.» What does stellar mean? | About the Moon | Quiet and shy | Lasting, wet and cold | *Excellent and outstanding
